    "result_text": "All 293 tests pass, including the new `Cp19Tests`.\n\nI implemented the audit logging in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`):\n\n- Added a dedicated logger `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");`.\n- After a successful `saveOwner`, it logs at INFO with the authenticated username, the new owner's id, and its membership number:\n  ```\n  AUDIT.info(\"Owner created by user={} ownerId={} membershipNumber={}\",\n      currentUsername(), owner.getId(), owner.getMembershipNumber());\n  ```\n- Added a `currentUsername()` helper that reads the principal from `SecurityContextHolder`, falling back to `\"anonymous\"` if unauthenticated.\n\nThe log line is emitted only on the success path (after all conflict/quota checks pass and the owner is persisted), so rejected requests produce no audit entry.",
